  "status": "SHORT_LOAD_GATES_PASSED_FULL_DURATION_PENDING",
  "scope": "Offline synthetic fixtures only. No host access, deployment, restart, resume, halt clearing or account mutation.",
  "changes": [
    "Timing records are bounded in memory and committed with ordinary fenced owner writes, with a final owner-close flush. Rollback retains pending versions; reports keep missing/unfinished traces explicit and count native commitments independently.",
    "Full entry requests and model budget reservations share one durable transaction before the model call. Original request expiry is checked after entering the restore fence. Admission rollback preserves the request without an admitted call; risk pause recognition is still committed.",
    "Every current SQLite cell is read. Tables with at least 256 rows reuse canonical JSON encodings in 256-row batches identified by SHA256 of typed scalar tuples. Pickle is used only for local serialization, never loading. The existing sorted canonical v1 hash and independent authority remain unchanged.",
    "The original 192 MiB encoding budget is divided into 160 MiB for row batches and 32 MiB for individual text. Both caches clear on a different restore authority. The four-MiB prefix limit, risk/model limits, freshness and native deadlines are unchanged."
  ],
  "evidence_limits": [
    "Short fixture uses 30,006 distinct diagnostic padding rows, not a reconstructed month of real account history.",
    "CPU affinity is one logical CPU; aggregate RSS is sampled against 1 GiB, not enforced by a kernel memory cgroup.",
    "Timing preparation latency excludes persistence; persistence is included in the owner transaction carrying the record. A crash before the next owner commit may leave a missing or RUNNING diagnostic.",
    "Matching batch fingerprints reuse encoding under the same SHA256 collision-resistance assumption as the authority hash; the canonical authority hash format is not migrated.",
    "Full-duration and month-growth acceptance remain pending. The installed host collector CONNECT failures remain unresolved."
  ],
